          "rationale": "The first cleanup change could erase the checkout for COVER_OUT=., so the step now resolves symlinks and rejects checkout ancestors before deleting contents. Sentinel regressions fail on 2e4a1b2 and pass here. Full scripts/ci also retains coverage in a new caller directory. Existing unrelated coverage contents still follow the previous clearing behavior, tracked separately as instructed.",
          "author": "fm/verilex-ci-tmp-leak"
        },
        {
          "newRange": [145, 146],
          "summary": "canary no longer advertises evidence that its exit trap removes.",
          "rationale": "The cleanup requirement covers failed canaries too, so retaining state or printing its deleted path would be wrong. Failure probes removed state and preserved the failure status.",
